      "item": "theoreticalsciences:quark_gluon_collider",
      "title": "Quark-Gluon Collider",
      "text": "A ring accelerator that smashes heavy nuclei into quark-gluon plasma.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Quarks are never seen alone - the strong force pulls harder the further apart they get. But smash heavy nuclei together hard enough and, for an instant, protons and neutrons melt into a soup of free quarks and gluons: the universe as it was a microsecond after the Big Bang."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
